concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-3-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3 3 An APP entity must not collect sensitive information about an"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-3-5 ;
    values:originalText "individual unless:  (a) the individual consents to the collection of the information and: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Australian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (i) if the entity is an agency—the information is reasonably necessary for, or directly related to, one or more of the entity’s functions or activities; or  (ii) if the entity is an organisation—the information is reasonably necessary for one or more of the entity’s functions or activities; or  (b) subclause 3.4 applies in relation to the information." ;
    skos:definition "individual unless:  (a) the individual consents to the collection of the information and: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Australian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (i) if the entity is an agency—the information is reasonably necessary for, or directly related to, one or more of the entity’s functions or activities; or  (ii) if the entity is an organisation—the information is reasonably necessary for one or more of the entity’s functions or activities; or  (b) subclause 3.4 applies in relation to the information."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c790ba545f5aaced487c3ece183676a6b910dd8a830c193fcf902469b4fb6ede" ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
