doc:sch-2-sec-6v-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "6V(1) Meaning of repayment history information" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a credit provider provides consumer credit to an individual, the following information about the consumer credit is repayment history information about the individual:  (a) whether or not the individual has met an obligation to make a monthly payment that is due and payable in relation to the consumer credit;  (b) the day on which the monthly payment is due and payable;  (c) if the individual makes the monthly payment after the day on which the payment is due and payable—the day on which the individual makes that payment." ;
    cof:pageNumber "77"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6v-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6V(2) Meaning of repayment history information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-6v-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The regulations may make provision in relation to:  (a) whether or not an individual has met an obligation to make a monthly payment that is due and payable in relation to consumer credit; and  (b) whether or not a payment is a monthly payment. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The regulations may make provision in relation to:  (a) whether or not an individual has met an obligation to make a monthly payment that is due and payable in relation to consumer credit; and  (b) whether or not a payment is a monthly payment. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3e9e13b23ff1ab39220218e636aaec320010a0cd121b4db59773fc0341c7062f" ;
