doc:sch-2-sec-20c-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20C(3) Collection of solicited credit information" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) the credit reporting body collects the credit information about the individual from a credit provider who is permitted under section 21D to disclose the information to the body; and  (b) the body collects the information in the course of carrying on a credit reporting business; and  (c) if the information is identification information about the individual—the body also collects from the provider, or already holds, credit information of another kind about the individual." ;
    cof:pageNumber "81"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20c-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20C(4) Collection of solicited credit information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20c-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) the credit reporting body:  (i) collects the credit information about the individual from an entity (other than a credit provider) in the course of carrying on a credit reporting business; and  (ii) knows, or believes on reasonable grounds, that the individual is at least 18 years old; and  (b) the information does not relate to an act, omission, matter or thing that occurred or existed before the individual turned 18; and  (c) if the information relates to consumer credit or commercial credit—the credit is or has been provided, or applied for, in Australia; and  (d) if the information is identification information about the individual—the body also collects from the entity, or already holds, credit information of another kind about the individual; and  (e) if the information is repayment history information about the individual—the body collects the information from another credit reporting body that has an Australian link." ;
    skos:definition "(4) Subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) the credit reporting body:  (i) collects the credit information about the individual from an entity (other than a credit provider) in the course of carrying on a credit reporting business; and  (ii) knows, or believes on reasonable grounds, that the individual is at least 18 years old; and  (b) the information does not relate to an act, omission, matter or thing that occurred or existed before the individual turned 18; and  (c) if the information relates to consumer credit or commercial credit—the credit is or has been provided, or applied for, in Australia; and  (d) if the information is identification information about the individual—the body also collects from the entity, or already holds, credit information of another kind about the individual; and  (e) if the information is repayment history information about the individual—the body collects the information from another credit reporting body that has an Australian link."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f92b8a072221ef335d9f3eac0751a2b6ca7655032ab92a5ecf05e644529031a4" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20c ;
    cof:pageNumber "81"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exemption from subsection (1) for certain credit reporting bodies" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.81" ;
