    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-20e-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20E(4) Use or disclosure of credit reporting information" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) However, if the credit reporting information is, or was derived from, repayment history information about the individual, the credit reporting body must not disclose the information under paragraph (3)(a) or (f) unless the recipient of the information is:  (a) a credit provider who is a licensee or is prescribed by the regulations; or  (b) a mortgage insurer. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units." ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20e-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20E(5) Use or disclosure of credit reporting information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20e-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If a credit reporting body discloses credit reporting information under this section, the body must make a written note of that disclosure. Civil penalty: 500 penalty units. Note: Other Acts may provide that the note must not be made (see for example the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002 and the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act 2006). No use or disclosure for the purposes of direct marketing" ;
    skos:definition "(5) If a credit reporting body discloses credit reporting information under this section, the body must make a written note of that disclosure. Civil penalty: 500 penalty units. Note: Other Acts may provide that the note must not be made (see for example the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002 and the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act 2006). No use or disclosure for the purposes of direct marketing"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "67ff7133d05bc4650032210fe94f3b6ad364c6b357f4d403d14103cbcade6b5a" ;
