concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20l a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20L Adoption of government related identifiers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20l ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information about an individual; and  (b) the information is a government related identifier of the individual; the body must not adopt the government related identifier as its own identifier of the individual. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the adoption of the government related identifier is required or authorised by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information about an individual; and  (b) the information is a government related identifier of the individual; the body must not adopt the government related identifier as its own identifier of the individual. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the adoption of the government related identifier is required or authorised by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order."@en ;
