concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20n-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20N(3) Quality of credit reporting information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20n-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Without limiting subsections (1) and (2), a credit reporting body must:  (a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the providers to ensure that credit information that they disclose to the body under section 21D is accurate, up-to-date and complete; and  (b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent person to determine whether those agreements are being complied with; and  (c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those agreements." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Without limiting subsections (1) and (2), a credit reporting body must:  (a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the providers to ensure that credit information that they disclose to the body under section 21D is accurate, up-to-date and complete; and  (b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent person to determine whether those agreements are being complied with; and  (c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those agreements."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "42d65549c9c8957c5346152bed29de7afb6b1066c3ba6c7335e7dcdac521af4c" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20n ;
    cof:pageNumber "93"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Ensure accuracy, completeness, and regular audits of credit information." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf> ;
