n) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (a) sets out the reasons for the refusal except to the extent that, having regard to the grounds for the refusal, it would be unreasonable to do so; and  (b) states that, if the access seeker is not satisfied with the response to the request, the access seeker may:  (i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme of which the body is a member; or  (ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V." ;
