doc:sch-2-sec-20s-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20S(1) Correction of credit reporting information" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) An individual may request a credit reporting body to correct personal information about the individual if:  (a) the personal information is:  (i) credit information about the individual; or  (ii) CRB derived information about the individual; or  (iii) CP derived information about the individual; and  (b) the body holds at least one kind of the personal information referred to in paragraph (a). Correction" ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20s-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20S(2) Correction of credit reporting information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20s-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the credit reporting body is satisfied that the personal information is inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or misleading, the body must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in the circumstances to correct the information within:  (a) the period of 30 days that starts on the day on which the request is made; or  (b) such longer period as the individual has agreed to in writing. Consultation" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If the credit reporting body is satisfied that the personal information is inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or misleading, the body must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in the circumstances to correct the information within:  (a) the period of 30 days that starts on the day on which the request is made; or  (b) such longer period as the individual has agreed to in writing. Consultation"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f7ec78ae49a3c7dc3c874d6b8457bb4607310441b6ad94e585f77ea45739d299" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20s ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Credit reporting body must correct inaccurate information within a specified period. Body must provide written notice of correction within a reasonable period." ;
    dc:description "written notice" ;
