    values:originalText "(3) If the credit reporting body considers that the body cannot be satisfied of the matter referred to in subsection (2) in relation to the personal information without consulting either or both of the following (the interested party):  (a) another credit reporting body that holds or held the information and that has an Australian link;  (b) a credit provider that holds or held the information and that has an Australian link; the body must consult that interested party, or those interested parties, about the individual’s request." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If the credit reporting body considers that the body cannot be satisfied of the matter referred to in subsection (2) in relation to the personal information without consulting either or both of the following (the interested party):  (a) another credit reporting body that holds or held the information and that has an Australian link;  (b) a credit provider that holds or held the information and that has an Australian link; the body must consult that interested party, or those interested parties, about the individual’s request."@en ;
