concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20v-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20V(4) Destruction etc. of credit reporting information after the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20v-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Subsection (2) does not apply if the credit reporting body is required by or under an Australian law, or a court/tribunal order, to retain the credit information. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Destruction etc. of CRB derived information" ;
    skos:definition "(4) Subsection (2) does not apply if the credit reporting body is required by or under an Australian law, or a court/tribunal order, to retain the credit information. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Destruction etc. of CRB derived information"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "35196c7d2c66f9946e7bad53775d23b1a2f6dbc42ced5621978a2e10a9bb4d2f" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20v ;
    cof:pageNumber "99"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Credit reporting body must retain credit information under certain circumstances." ;
