concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20w a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20W Retention period for credit information—general"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20w ;
    values:originalText "The following table sets out the retention period for credit information:  (a) that is information of a kind referred to in an item of the table; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (b) that is held by a credit reporting body.  Retention period Item If the credit information is ... the retention period for the information is ... consumer credit liability information the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the consumer credit to which the information relates is terminated or otherwise ceases to be in force. repayment history information the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the monthly payment to which the information relates is due and payable. information of a kind referred to in paragraph 6N(d) or (e) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the information request to which the information relates is made. default information the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the information. payment information the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the default information to which the payment information relates. new arrangement information within the meaning of subsection 6S(1) the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the default information referred to in that subsection. new arrangement information within the meaning of subsection 6S(2) the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the information about the opinion referred to in that subsection. court proceedings information the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the judgement to which the information relates is made or given. information of a kind referred to in paragraph 6N(l) the period of 7 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the information. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15" ;
    skos:definition "The following table sets out the retention period for credit information:  (a) that is information of a kind referred to in an item of the table; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (b) that is held by a credit reporting body.  Retention period Item If the credit information is ... the retention period for the information is ... consumer credit liability information the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the consumer credit to which the information relates is terminated or otherwise ceases to be in force. repayment history information the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the monthly payment to which the information relates is due and payable. information of a kind referred to in paragraph 6N(d) or (e) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the information request to which the information relates is made. default information the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the information. payment information the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the default information to which the payment information relates. new arrangement information within the meaning of subsection 6S(1) the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the default information referred to in that subsection. new arrangement information within the meaning of subsection 6S(2) the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the information about the opinion referred to in that subsection. court proceedings information the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the judgement to which the information relates is made or given. information of a kind referred to in paragraph 6N(l) the period of 7 years that starts on the day on which the cr"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0e301423726ea3d75e570d3d6388c225df4c1d700c76cd0970f94cadf14d73e6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "100"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Retention period for credit information—general" ;
