doc:sch-2-sec-20w a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20W Retention period for credit information—general" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The following table sets out the retention period for credit information:  (a) that is information of a kind referred to in an item of the table; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (b) that is held by a credit reporting body.  Retention period Item If the credit information is ... the retention period for the information is ... consumer credit liability information the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the consumer credit to which the information relates is terminated or otherwise ceases to be in force. repayment history information the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the monthly payment to which the information relates is due and payable. information of a kind referred to in paragraph 6N(d) or (e) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the information request to which the information relates is made. default information the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the information. payment information the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the default information to which the payment information relates. new arrangement information within the meaning of subsection 6S(1) the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the default information referred to in that subsection. new arrangement information within the meaning of subsection 6S(2) the period of 2 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the information about the opinion referred to in that subsection. court proceedings information the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the judgement to which the information relates is made or given. information of a kind referred to in paragraph 6N(l) the period of 7 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the information. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15" ;
    cof:pageNumber "100"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20x a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20X Retention period for credit information—personal insolvency"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20x ;
    values:originalText "information  (1) The following table has effect:  Item If personal insolvency information relates to ... the retention period for the information is whichever of the following periods ends later ... a bankruptcy of an individual (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the individual becomes a bankrupt; (b) the period of 2 years that starts on the day the bankruptcy ends. a personal insolvency agreement to which item 3 of this table does not apply (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is executed; (b) the period of 2 years that starts on the day the agreement is terminated or set aside under the Bankruptcy Act. a personal insolvency agreement in relation to which a certificate has been signed under section 232 of the Bankruptcy Act (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is executed; (b) the period that ends on the day on which the certificate is signed. a debt agreement to which item 5 of this table does not apply (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is made; (b) the period of 2 years that starts on the day: (i) the agreement is terminated under the Bankruptcy Act; or (ii) an order declaring that all the agreement is void is made under that Act. a debt agreement that ends under section 185N of the Bankruptcy Act (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is made; (b) the period that ends on the day on which the agreement ends. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Debt agreement proposals  (2) If personal insolvency information relates to a debt agreement proposal, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which:  (a) the proposal is withdrawn; or  (b) the proposal is not accepted under section 185EC of the Bankruptcy Act; or  (c) the acceptance of the proposal for processing is cancelled under section 185ED of that Act; or  (d) the proposal lapses under section 185G of that Act. Control of property  (3) If personal insolvency information relates to a direction given, or an order made, under section 50 of the Bankruptcy Act, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which the control of the property to which the direction or order relates ends. Note: See subsection 50(1B) of the Bankruptcy Act for when the control of the property ends.  (4) If the personal insolvency information relates to an authority signed under section 188 of the Bankruptcy Act, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which the property to which the authority relates is no longer subject to control under Division 2 of Part X of that Act. Interpretation  (5) An expression used in this section that is also used in the Bankruptcy Act has the same meaning in this section as it has in that Act." ;
    skos:definition "information  (1) The following table has effect:  Item If personal insolvency information relates to ... the retention period for the information is whichever of the following periods ends later ... a bankruptcy of an individual (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the individual becomes a bankrupt; (b) the period of 2 years that starts on the day the bankruptcy ends. a personal insolvency agreement to which item 3 of this table does not apply (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is executed; (b) the period of 2 years that starts on the day the agreement is terminated or set aside under the Bankruptcy Act. a personal insolvency agreement in relation to which a certificate has been signed under section 232 of the Bankruptcy Act (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is executed; (b) the period that ends on the day on which the certificate is signed. a debt agreement to which item 5 of this table does not apply (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is made; (b) the period of 2 years that starts on the day: (i) the agreement is terminated under the Bankruptcy Act; or (ii) an order declaring that all the agreement is void is made under that Act. a debt agreement that ends under section 185N of the Bankruptcy Act (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is made; (b) the period that ends on the day on which the agreement ends. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Debt agreement proposals  (2) If personal insolvency information relates to a debt agreement proposal, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which:  (a) the proposal is withdrawn; or  (b) the proposal is not accepted under section 185EC of the Bankruptcy Act; or  (c) the acceptance of the"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "dea7111a8406e27cfc8bf5f49c5d40898402b0b584b3285f069170a36f9eec31" ;
    cof:pageNumber "102"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20x-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20x-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20x-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20x-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20x-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.102" .
doc:sch-2-sec-20x a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20X Retention period for credit information—personal insolvency" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "information  (1) The following table has effect:  Item If personal insolvency information relates to ... the retention period for the information is whichever of the following periods ends later ... a bankruptcy of an individual (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the individual becomes a bankrupt; (b) the period of 2 years that starts on the day the bankruptcy ends. a personal insolvency agreement to which item 3 of this table does not apply (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is executed; (b) the period of 2 years that starts on the day the agreement is terminated or set aside under the Bankruptcy Act. a personal insolvency agreement in relation to which a certificate has been signed under section 232 of the Bankruptcy Act (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is executed; (b) the period that ends on the day on which the certificate is signed. a debt agreement to which item 5 of this table does not apply (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is made; (b) the period of 2 years that starts on the day: (i) the agreement is terminated under the Bankruptcy Act; or (ii) an order declaring that all the agreement is void is made under that Act. a debt agreement that ends under section 185N of the Bankruptcy Act (a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is made; (b) the period that ends on the day on which the agreement ends. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Debt agreement proposals  (2) If personal insolvency information relates to a debt agreement proposal, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which:  (a) the proposal is withdrawn; or  (b) the proposal is not accepted under section 185EC of the Bankruptcy Act; or  (c) the acceptance of the proposal for processing is cancelled under section 185ED of that Act; or  (d) the proposal lapses under section 185G of that Act. Control of property  (3) If personal insolvency information relates to a direction given, or an order made, under section 50 of the Bankruptcy Act, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which the control of the property to which the direction or order relates ends. Note: See subsection 50(1B) of the Bankruptcy Act for when the control of the property ends.  (4) If the personal insolvency information relates to an authority signed under section 188 of the Bankruptcy Act, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which the property to which the authority relates is no longer subject to control under Division 2 of Part X of that Act. Interpretation  (5) An expression used in this section that is also used in the Bankruptcy Act has the same meaning in this section as it has in that Act." ;
    cof:pageNumber "102"^^xsd:integer .

