concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20x-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20X(2) Retention period for credit information—personal insolvency"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20x-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If personal insolvency information relates to a debt agreement proposal, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which:  (a) the proposal is withdrawn; or  (b) the proposal is not accepted under section 185EC of the Bankruptcy Act; or  (c) the acceptance of the proposal for processing is cancelled under section 185ED of that Act; or  (d) the proposal lapses under section 185G of that Act. Control of property" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If personal insolvency information relates to a debt agreement proposal, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which:  (a) the proposal is withdrawn; or  (b) the proposal is not accepted under section 185EC of the Bankruptcy Act; or  (c) the acceptance of the proposal for processing is cancelled under section 185ED of that Act; or  (d) the proposal lapses under section 185G of that Act. Control of property"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7bcd8623b872e999b35caea34136b01c4183ce40896c82abb3f4aebe60415b6f" ;
