concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20x-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20X(3) Retention period for credit information—personal insolvency"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20x-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If personal insolvency information relates to a direction given, or an order made, under section 50 of the Bankruptcy Act, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which the control of the property to which the direction or order relates ends. Note: See subsection 50(1B) of the Bankruptcy Act for when the control of the property ends." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If personal insolvency information relates to a direction given, or an order made, under section 50 of the Bankruptcy Act, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which the control of the property to which the direction or order relates ends. Note: See subsection 50(1B) of the Bankruptcy Act for when the control of the property ends."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "43ce83d2b5fb694c93c8744e988771b17d298ce6e848f18a63ec79696cc22590" ;
