concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20x-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20X(4) Retention period for credit information—personal insolvency"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20x-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the personal insolvency information relates to an authority signed under section 188 of the Bankruptcy Act, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which the property to which the authority relates is no longer subject to control under Division 2 of Part X of that Act. Interpretation" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the personal insolvency information relates to an authority signed under section 188 of the Bankruptcy Act, the retention period for the information is the period that ends on the day on which the property to which the authority relates is no longer subject to control under Division 2 of Part X of that Act. Interpretation"@en ;
