doc:sch-2-sec-21d-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "21D(5) Disclosure of credit information to a credit reporting body" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) Despite paragraph (3)(a), consumer credit liability information about the individual may relate to consumer credit that was entered into on a day before the individual turned 18, so long as the consumer credit was not terminated, or did not otherwise cease to be in force, on a day before the individual turned 18. Written note of disclosure" ;
    cof:pageNumber "111"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21d-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21D(6) Disclosure of credit information to a credit reporting body"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21d-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) If a credit provider discloses credit information under this section, the provider must make a written note of that disclosure. Civil penalty: 500 penalty units. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Interaction with the Australian Privacy Principles" ;
    skos:definition "(6) If a credit provider discloses credit information under this section, the provider must make a written note of that disclosure. Civil penalty: 500 penalty units. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Interaction with the Australian Privacy Principles"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ebabde7b9dc45546992df53f6982eec2496c1b07eb3d5f71ba79b6f82fc17297" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21d ;
