doc:sch-2-sec-21e a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "21E Payment information must be disclosed to a credit reporting" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "body  If:  (a) a credit provider has disclosed default information about an individual to a credit reporting body under section 21D; and  (b) after the default information was disclosed, the amount of the overdue payment to which the information relates is paid; the provider must, within a reasonable period after the amount is paid, disclose payment information about the amount to the body under that section. Civil penalty: 500 penalty units." ;
    cof:pageNumber "113"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21F Limitation on the disclosure of credit information during a ban"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21f ;
    values:originalText "period  (1) This section applies if:  (a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information about an individual; and  (b) a credit provider requests the body to disclose the information to the provider for the purpose of assessing an application for consumer credit made to the provider by the individual, or a person purporting to be the individual; and  (c) the body is not permitted to disclose the information because there is a ban period for the information; and  (d) during the ban period, the provider provides the consumer credit to which the application relates to the individual, or the person purporting to be the individual.  (2) If the credit provider holds credit information about the individual that relates to the consumer credit, the provider must not, despite sections 21D and 21E, disclose the information to a credit reporting body. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units.  (3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the credit provider has taken such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify the identity of the individual. Subdivision D—Dealing with credit eligibility information etc." ;
    skos:definition "period  (1) This section applies if:  (a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information about an individual; and  (b) a credit provider requests the body to disclose the information to the provider for the purpose of assessing an application for consumer credit made to the provider by the individual, or a person purporting to be the individual; and  (c) the body is not permitted to disclose the information because there is a ban period for the information; and  (d) during the ban period, the provider provides the consumer credit to which the application relates to the individual, or the person purporting to be the individual.  (2) If the credit provider holds credit information about the individual that relates to the consumer credit, the provider must not, despite sections 21D and 21E, disclose the information to a credit reporting body. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units.  (3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the credit provider has taken such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify the identity of the individual. Subdivision D—Dealing with credit eligibility information etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "514cb13f603464f97849ba88d2d4f9698003a9323de9b7a3d162ef76f6998122" ;
    cof:pageNumber "113"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21f-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21f-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21f-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.113" .
doc:sch-2-sec-21f a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "21F Limitation on the disclosure of credit information during a ban" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "period  (1) This section applies if:  (a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information about an individual; and  (b) a credit provider requests the body to disclose the information to the provider for the purpose of assessing an application for consumer credit made to the provider by the individual, or a person purporting to be the individual; and  (c) the body is not permitted to disclose the information because there is a ban period for the information; and  (d) during the ban period, the provider provides the consumer credit to which the application relates to the individual, or the person purporting to be the individual.  (2) If the credit provider holds credit information about the individual that relates to the consumer credit, the provider must not, despite sections 21D and 21E, disclose the information to a credit reporting body. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units.  (3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the credit provider has taken such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify the identity of the individual. Subdivision D—Dealing with credit eligibility information etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "113"^^xsd:integer .

