    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if:  (a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information about an individual; and  (b) a credit provider requests the body to disclose the information to the provider for the purpose of assessing an application for consumer credit made to the provider by the individual, or a person purporting to be the individual; and  (c) the body is not permitted to disclose the information because there is a ban period for the information; and  (d) during the ban period, the provider provides the consumer credit to which the application relates to the individual, or the person purporting to be the individual."@en ;
