    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the credit provider holds credit information about the individual that relates to the consumer credit, the provider must not, despite sections 21D and 21E, disclose the information to a credit reporting body. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units." ;
    cof:pageNumber "113"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21f-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21F(3) Limitation on the disclosure of credit information during a ban"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21f-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the credit provider has taken such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify the identity of the individual. Subdivision D—Dealing with credit eligibility information etc." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the credit provider has taken such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify the identity of the individual. Subdivision D—Dealing with credit eligibility information etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "078baab8fa6f6ac2de978cd61e6a35748551dd0b27a71afb3ffd77e51fa9268e" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21f ;
    cof:pageNumber "113"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Credit provider must verify identity of individual before disclosing credit information." ;
