doc:sch-2-sec-21j-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "21J(2) Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The consent of the individual under paragraph (1)(c):  (a) must be given in writing unless:  (i) the disclosure of the information to the recipient is for the purpose of assessing an application for consumer credit or commercial credit made to the recipient; and  (ii) the application has not been made in writing; and  (b) must be given to the credit provider or recipient. Agents of credit providers" ;
    cof:pageNumber "118"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21j-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21J(3) Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21j-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information about an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the individual if:  (a) the provider is acting as an agent of another credit provider that has an Australian link; and  (b) while the provider is so acting, the provider is a credit provider under subsection 6H(1); and  (c) the provider discloses the information to the other credit provider in the provider’s capacity as such an agent. Securitisation arrangements etc." ;
    skos:definition "(3) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information about an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the individual if:  (a) the provider is acting as an agent of another credit provider that has an Australian link; and  (b) while the provider is so acting, the provider is a credit provider under subsection 6H(1); and  (c) the provider discloses the information to the other credit provider in the provider’s capacity as such an agent. Securitisation arrangements etc."@en ;
