doc:sch-2-sec-21j-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "21J(4) Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information about an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the individual if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (a) the provider is a credit provider under subsection 6J(1) in relation to credit; and  (b) the credit has been provided by, or is credit for which an application has been made to, another credit provider (the original credit provider) that has an Australian link; and  (c) the original credit provider is not a credit provider under that subsection; and  (d) the information is disclosed to:  (i) the original credit provider; or  (ii) another credit provider that is a credit provider under that subsection in relation to the credit and that has an Australian link; and  (e) the disclosure of the information is reasonably necessary for:  (i) purchasing, funding or managing, or processing an application for, the credit by means of a securitisation arrangement; or  (ii) undertaking credit enhancement in relation to the credit. Mortgage credit secured by the same real property" ;
    cof:pageNumber "118"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21j-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21J(5) Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21j-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information about an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the individual if:  (a) the disclosure is to another credit provider that has an Australian link; and  (b) both credit providers have provided mortgage credit to the individual in relation to which the same real property forms all or part of the security; and  (c) the individual is at least 60 days overdue in making a payment in relation to the mortgage credit provided by either provider; and  (d) the information is disclosed for the purpose of either provider deciding what action to take in relation to the overdue payment. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  21K  Permitted CP disclosures relating to guarantees etc. Offer to act as a guarantor etc." ;
    skos:definition "(5) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information about an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the individual if:  (a) the disclosure is to another credit provider that has an Australian link; and  (b) both credit providers have provided mortgage credit to the individual in relation to which the same real property forms all or part of the security; and  (c) the individual is at least 60 days overdue in making a payment in relation to the mortgage credit provided by either provider; and  (d) the information is disclosed for the purpose of either provider deciding what action to take in relation to the overdue payment. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 2  Credit reporting  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  21K  Permitted CP disclosures relating to guarantees etc. Offer to act as a guarantor etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fd316c08851dcc3f3f35e5bae707d6c28f8957018f32a85ec1bc8c0b3c72289a" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21j ;
    cof:pageNumber "118"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers" ;
