doc:sch-2-sec-21j-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "21J(2) Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The consent of the individual under paragraph (1)(d) must be given in writing unless:  (a) if subparagraph (1)(a)(i) applies—the application for the credit was not made in writing; or  (b) if subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) applies—the application for the credit has not been made in writing. Guarantors etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "118"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21j-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21J(3) Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21j-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information about an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the individual if:  (a) the disclosure is to a person who:  (i) is a guarantor in relation to credit provided by the provider to the individual; or  (ii) has provided property as security for such credit; and  (b) the person has an Australian link; and  (c) either:  (i) the individual expressly consents to the disclosure of the information to the person; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (ii) if subparagraph (a)(i) applies—the information is disclosed to the person for a purpose related to the enforcement, or proposed enforcement, of the guarantee." ;
    skos:definition "(3) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information about an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the individual if:  (a) the disclosure is to a person who:  (i) is a guarantor in relation to credit provided by the provider to the individual; or  (ii) has provided property as security for such credit; and  (b) the person has an Australian link; and  (c) either:  (i) the individual expressly consents to the disclosure of the information to the person; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (ii) if subparagraph (a)(i) applies—the information is disclosed to the person for a purpose related to the enforcement, or proposed enforcement, of the guarantee."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "47c0d9759e59ede2d673f2a10581bd9bcf0819cd20167874763bc92224b2b3b2" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21j ;
    cof:pageNumber "118"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosure of credit eligibility information is permitted to certain individuals under specific conditions. Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
