    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if:  (a) a credit provider refuses an application for consumer credit made in Australia:  (i) by an individual; or  (ii) jointly by an individual and one or more other persons (the other applicants); and  (b) the refusal is based wholly or partly on credit eligibility information about one or more of the following:  (i) the individual;  (ii) a person who is proposing to act as a guarantor in relation to the consumer credit;  (iii) if the application is an application of a kind referred to in subparagraph (a)(ii)—one of the other applicants; and  (c) a credit reporting body disclosed the relevant credit reporting information to the provider for the purposes of assessing the application." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if:  (a) a credit provider refuses an application for consumer credit made in Australia:  (i) by an individual; or  (ii) jointly by an individual and one or more other persons (the other applicants); and  (b) the refusal is based wholly or partly on credit eligibility information about one or more of the following:  (i) the individual;  (ii) a person who is proposing to act as a guarantor in relation to the consumer credit;  (iii) if the application is an application of a kind referred to in subparagraph (a)(ii)—one of the other applicants; and  (c) a credit reporting body disclosed the relevant credit reporting information to the provider for the purposes of assessing the application."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "051bf03fe66e5e2bc40b551b16d957bd20b88685d0d5ea57ccfbef0866e317a3" ;
