concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21r a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21R False or misleading credit information or credit eligibility"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21r ;
    values:originalText "information Offences  (1) A credit provider commits an offence if:  (a) the provider discloses credit information under section 21D; and  (b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  (2) A credit provider commits an offence if:  (a) the provider uses or discloses credit eligibility information under this Division; and  (b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular. Penalty: 200 penalty units. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Civil penalties  (3) A credit provider must not disclose credit information under section 21D if the information is false or misleading in a material particular. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units.  (4) A credit provider must not use or disclose credit eligibility information under this Division if the information is false or misleading in a material particular. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "information Offences  (1) A credit provider commits an offence if:  (a) the provider discloses credit information under section 21D; and  (b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  (2) A credit provider commits an offence if:  (a) the provider uses or discloses credit eligibility information under this Division; and  (b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular. Penalty: 200 penalty units. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  Civil penalties  (3) A credit provider must not disclose credit information under section 21D if the information is false or misleading in a material particular. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units.  (4) A credit provider must not use or disclose credit eligibility information under this Division if the information is false or misleading in a material particular. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units."@en ;
