concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21t-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21T(7) Access to credit eligibility information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21t-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) If the provider refuses to give access to the information because of subsection (2), the provider must give the access seeker a written notice that:  (a) sets out the reasons for the refusal except to the extent that, having regard to the grounds for the refusal, it would be unreasonable to do so; and  (b) states that, if the access seeker is not satisfied with the response to the request, the access seeker may:  (i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme of which the provider is a member; or  (ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V. Interaction with the Australian Privacy Principles" ;
    skos:definition "(7) If the provider refuses to give access to the information because of subsection (2), the provider must give the access seeker a written notice that:  (a) sets out the reasons for the refusal except to the extent that, having regard to the grounds for the refusal, it would be unreasonable to do so; and  (b) states that, if the access seeker is not satisfied with the response to the request, the access seeker may:  (i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme of which the provider is a member; or  (ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V. Interaction with the Australian Privacy Principles"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "30bd8da9868dd1c3f40f9e0b058c9c016ce9f426e37ea642fc491d177fa7f00d" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21t ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Provider must give written notice if refusing access to credit eligibility information" ;
    dc:description "written notice" ;
