    skos:definition "(1) An individual may complain to a credit reporting body about an act or practice engaged in by the body that may be a breach of either of the following provisions in relation to the individual:  (a) a provision of this Part (other than section 20R or 20T);  (b) a provision of the registered CR code (other than a provision that relates to that section). Note: A complaint about a breach of section 20R or 20T, or a provision of the registered CR code that relates to that section, may be made to the Commissioner under Part V."@en ;
