concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-23b-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23B(4) Dealing with complaints"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-23b-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) After investigating the complaint, the respondent must, within the period referred to in subsection (5), make a decision about the complaint and give the individual a written notice that:  (a) sets out the decision; and  (b) states that, if the individual is not satisfied with the decision, the individual may:  (i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme of which the respondent is a member; or  (ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V." ;
    skos:definition "(4) After investigating the complaint, the respondent must, within the period referred to in subsection (5), make a decision about the complaint and give the individual a written notice that:  (a) sets out the decision; and  (b) states that, if the individual is not satisfied with the decision, the individual may:  (i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme of which the respondent is a member; or  (ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a1d84566b262ac741e552984893ba059640837d2ec99e18b9f789b51ae3c1c0a" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-23b ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Respondent must make a decision and give written notice to individual within specified period." ;
    dc:description "written notice" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
