doc:sch-2-sec-23b-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "23B(4) Dealing with complaints" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) After investigating the complaint, the respondent must, within the period referred to in subsection (5), make a decision about the complaint and give the individual a written notice that:  (a) sets out the decision; and  (b) states that, if the individual is not satisfied with the decision, the individual may:  (i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme of which the respondent is a member; or  (ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V." ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-23b-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23B(5) Dealing with complaints"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-23b-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) The period for the purposes of subsection (4) is:  (a) the period of 30 days that starts on the day on which the complaint is made; or  (b) such longer period as the individual has agreed to in writing. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15" ;
    skos:definition "(5) The period for the purposes of subsection (4) is:  (a) the period of 30 days that starts on the day on which the complaint is made; or  (b) such longer period as the individual has agreed to in writing. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "762843c9847d8f1c4be2c3c01de93d5f098086cfbaac5636d8af06f78e1abbb1" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-23b ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines a period for complaints" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
