concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-25-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "25 Compensation orders"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-25-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Federal Court or the Federal Magistrates Court may order an entity to compensate a person for loss or damage (including injury to the person’s feelings or humiliation) suffered by the person if:  (a) either:  (i) a civil penalty order has been made against the entity for a contravention of a civil penalty provision (other than section 13G); or  (ii) the entity is found guilty of an offence against this Part; and  (b) that loss or damage resulted from the contravention or commission of the offence. The order must specify the amount of compensation.  (2) The court may make the order only if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (a) the person applies for an order under this section; and  (b) the application is made within 6 years of the day the cause of action that relates to the contravention or commission of the offence accrued.  (3) If the court makes the order, the amount of compensation specified in the order that is to be paid to the person may be recovered as a debt due to the person." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Federal Court or the Federal Magistrates Court may order an entity to compensate a person for loss or damage (including injury to the person’s feelings or humiliation) suffered by the person if:  (a) either:  (i) a civil penalty order has been made against the entity for a contravention of a civil penalty provision (other than section 13G); or  (ii) the entity is found guilty of an offence against this Part; and  (b) that loss or damage resulted from the contravention or commission of the offence. The order must specify the amount of compensation.  (2) The court may make the order only if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Credit reporting  Schedule 2  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (a) the person applies for an order under this section; and  (b) the application is made within 6 years of the day the cause of action that relates to the contravention or commission of the offence accrued.  (3) If the court makes the order, the amount of compensation specified in the order that is to be paid to the person may be recovered as a debt due to the person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1836f808d00f1253bf7fc114b39860f5494403eafe290fcf465baedd7f4d5d01" ;
    cof:pageNumber "146"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-25-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-25-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-25-2-ss-3 ;
