concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26B What is a registered APP code"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-26b ;
    values:originalText "(1) A registered APP code is an APP code:  (a) that is included on the Codes Register; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 3  Privacy codes  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (b) that is in force.  (2) A registered APP code is a legislative instrument.  (3) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003, a registered APP code may be expressed to take effect before the date it is registered under that Act. Note: An APP code cannot come into force before it is included on the Codes Register: see paragraph 26C(2)(c)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A registered APP code is an APP code:  (a) that is included on the Codes Register; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 3  Privacy codes  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (b) that is in force.  (2) A registered APP code is a legislative instrument.  (3) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003, a registered APP code may be expressed to take effect before the date it is registered under that Act. Note: An APP code cannot come into force before it is included on the Codes Register: see paragraph 26C(2)(c)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d0c44fa4fce8c3bbdd70774eba8c7350068ba4c72c1d52a27b221d406555ed8c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "153"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b-ss-1 ;
