concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26p a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26P Development of CR code by CR code developers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-26p ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, request a CR code developer to develop a CR code and apply to the Commissioner for the code to be registered.  (2) The request must:  (a) specify the period within which the request must be complied with; and  (b) set out the effect of section 26L.  (3) The period:  (a) must run for at least 120 days from the date the request is made; and  (b) may be extended by the Commissioner. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 3  Privacy codes  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (4) The request may:  (a) specify one or more matters that the CR code must deal with; and  (b) specify the credit providers, or a class of credit providers, that should be bound by the code; and  (c) specify the other entities, or a class of other entities, subject to Part IIIA that should be bound by the code.  (5) The Commissioner must make a copy of the request publicly available as soon as practicable after the request is made." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, request a CR code developer to develop a CR code and apply to the Commissioner for the code to be registered.  (2) The request must:  (a) specify the period within which the request must be complied with; and  (b) set out the effect of section 26L.  (3) The period:  (a) must run for at least 120 days from the date the request is made; and  (b) may be extended by the Commissioner. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Schedule 3  Privacy codes  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012  Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (4) The request may:  (a) specify one or more matters that the CR code must deal with; and  (b) specify the credit providers, or a class of credit providers, that should be bound by the code; and  (c) specify the other entities, or a class of other entities, subject to Part IIIA that should be bound by the code.  (5) The Commissioner must make a copy of the request publicly available as soon as practicable after the request is made."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "da691b2cc62e672e12d348522180cb6c3049294e6b6bfe667b6fe53d8b1fee25" ;
    cof:pageNumber "161"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26p-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26p-ss-2 ;
