concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-35 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "35 Subsections 12B(1) and (2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-35 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsections, substitute:  (1) Without limiting its effect apart from this section, this Act has effect in relation to the following (the regulated entities) as provided by this section:  (a) an agency;  (b) an organisation;  (c) a small business operator;  (d) a body politic. Note: Subsection 27(4) applies in relation to an investigation of an act or practice referred to in subsection 29(1) of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010.  (2) This Act also has the effect it would have if its operation in relation to regulated entities were expressly confined to an operation to give effect to the following:  (a) the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights done at New York on 16 December 1966 ([1980] ATS 23), and in particular Articles 17 and 24(1) of the Covenant;  (b) Article 16 of the Convention on the Rights of the Child done at New York on 20 November 1989 ([1991] ATS 4). Note: In 2012, the text of the Covenant and Convention in the Australian Treaty Series was accessible through the Australian Treaties Library on the AustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au)." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsections, substitute:  (1) Without limiting its effect apart from this section, this Act has effect in relation to the following (the regulated entities) as provided by this section:  (a) an agency;  (b) an organisation;  (c) a small business operator;  (d) a body politic. Note: Subsection 27(4) applies in relation to an investigation of an act or practice referred to in subsection 29(1) of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010.  (2) This Act also has the effect it would have if its operation in relation to regulated entities were expressly confined to an operation to give effect to the following:  (a) the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights done at New York on 16 December 1966 ([1980] ATS 23), and in particular Articles 17 and 24(1) of the Covenant;  (b) Article 16 of the Convention on the Rights of the Child done at New York on 20 November 1989 ([1991] ATS 4). Note: In 2012, the text of the Covenant and Convention in the Australian Treaty Series was accessible through the Australian Treaties Library on the AustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "45006b563b2fa2182b7ea81cca2aac16faa404d7946d1c0f51f91fbff6cf069d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "173"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-35-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-35-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.173" .
