concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "27 Functions of the Commissioner"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-27-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner has the following functions:  (a) the functions that are conferred on the Commissioner by or under:  (i) this Act; or  (ii) any other law of the Commonwealth;  (b) the guidance related functions;  (c) the monitoring related functions;  (d) the advice related functions;  (e) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of any of the above functions. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (2) The Commissioner has power to do all things necessary or convenient to be done for, or in connection with, the performance of the Commissioner’s functions.  (3) Without limiting subsection (2), the Commissioner may establish a panel of persons with expertise in relation to a particular matter to assist the Commissioner in performing any of the Commissioner’s functions.  (4) Section 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010, rather than section 12B of this Act, applies in relation to an investigation of an act or practice referred to in subsection 29(1) of that Act in the same way as it applies to Parts 3 and 4 of that Act. Note: Section 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010 deals with the additional effect of Parts 3 and 4 of that Act." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner has the following functions:  (a) the functions that are conferred on the Commissioner by or under:  (i) this Act; or  (ii) any other law of the Commonwealth;  (b) the guidance related functions;  (c) the monitoring related functions;  (d) the advice related functions;  (e) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of any of the above functions. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (2) The Commissioner has power to do all things necessary or convenient to be done for, or in connection with, the performance of the Commissioner’s functions.  (3) Without limiting subsection (2), the Commissioner may establish a panel of persons with expertise in relation to a particular matter to assist the Commissioner in performing any of the Commissioner’s functions.  (4) Section 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010, rather than section 12B of this Act, applies in relation to an investigation of an act or practice referred to in subsection 29(1) of that Act in the same way as it applies to Parts 3 and 4 of that Act. Note: Section 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010 deals with the additional effect of Parts 3 and 4 of that Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0897147789da389b629a66d1061878932805e33fa157ab4485aef96b4d471132" ;
    cof:pageNumber "178"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.178" .
doc:sch-4-sec-27-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "27 Functions of the Commissioner" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner has the following functions:  (a) the functions that are conferred on the Commissioner by or under:  (i) this Act; or  (ii) any other law of the Commonwealth;  (b) the guidance related functions;  (c) the monitoring related functions;  (d) the advice related functions;  (e) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of any of the above functions. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (2) The Commissioner has power to do all things necessary or convenient to be done for, or in connection with, the performance of the Commissioner’s functions.  (3) Without limiting subsection (2), the Commissioner may establish a panel of persons with expertise in relation to a particular matter to assist the Commissioner in performing any of the Commissioner’s functions.  (4) Section 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010, rather than section 12B of this Act, applies in relation to an investigation of an act or practice referred to in subsection 29(1) of that Act in the same way as it applies to Parts 3 and 4 of that Act. Note: Section 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010 deals with the additional effect of Parts 3 and 4 of that Act." ;
    cof:pageNumber "178"^^xsd:integer .

