    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a complaint about an act or practice is made under section 36; and  (b) the Commissioner considers it is reasonably possible that the complaint may be conciliated successfully; the Commissioner must make a reasonable attempt to conciliate the complaint. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15"@en ;
