concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80x a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "80X Civil enforcement of penalty"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-80x ;
    values:originalText "(1) A pecuniary penalty is a debt payable to the Commonwealth.  (2) The Commonwealth may enforce a civil penalty order as if it were an order made in civil proceedings against the entity to recover a debt due by the entity. The debt arising from the order is taken to be a judgement debt. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A pecuniary penalty is a debt payable to the Commonwealth.  (2) The Commonwealth may enforce a civil penalty order as if it were an order made in civil proceedings against the entity to recover a debt due by the entity. The debt arising from the order is taken to be a judgement debt. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "093faa1ab6d98b7b6f4b45e75cf517c5807532bee7a15c11cfd7422a5c2008c2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "208"^^xsd:integer ;
