concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "96 Review by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-96-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of the following decisions of the Commissioner:  (a) a decision under subsection 26H(1) not to register an APP code developed by an APP code developer;  (b) a decision under subsection 26S(1) not to register a CR code developed by a CR code developer;  (c) a decision under subsection 52(1) or (1A) to make a determination; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (d) a decision under subsection 73(1A) to dismiss an application;  (e) a decision under section 95 to refuse to approve the issue of guidelines;  (f) a decision under subsection 95A(2) or (4) or 95AA(2) to refuse to approve guidelines;  (g) a decision under subsection 95A(6) to revoke an approval of guidelines.  (2) An application under paragraph (1)(a) may only be made by the APP code developer that developed the APP code.  (3) An application under paragraph (1)(b) may only be made by the CR code developer that developed the CR code." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of the following decisions of the Commissioner:  (a) a decision under subsection 26H(1) not to register an APP code developed by an APP code developer;  (b) a decision under subsection 26S(1) not to register a CR code developed by a CR code developer;  (c) a decision under subsection 52(1) or (1A) to make a determination; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (d) a decision under subsection 73(1A) to dismiss an application;  (e) a decision under section 95 to refuse to approve the issue of guidelines;  (f) a decision under subsection 95A(2) or (4) or 95AA(2) to refuse to approve guidelines;  (g) a decision under subsection 95A(6) to revoke an approval of guidelines.  (2) An application under paragraph (1)(a) may only be made by the APP code developer that developed the APP code.  (3) An application under paragraph (1)(b) may only be made by the CR code developer that developed the CR code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fb186d7914a0eb3faa471267d1cd114dab0ea10c5fd67889ad0a4cef26fceada" ;
    cof:pageNumber "212"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96-2-ss-3 ;
