concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-18-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "18 Pre-commencement acts and practices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-18-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This item applies if:  (a) before the commencement time, an act was done, or a practice was engaged in, by an agency or organisation; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Application, transitional and savings provisions  Schedule 6 Provisions relating to other matters  Part 7  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (b) the act or practice may be an interference with the privacy of an individual under section 13 or 13A of the Privacy Act (as in force immediately before that time); and  (c) immediately before that time:  (i) the individual has not made a complaint about the act or practice to the Commissioner under section 36 of that Act; and  (ii) the Commissioner has not decided to investigate the act or practice under subsection 40(2) of that Act. (2) Despite the amendments of the Privacy Act made by this Act, the individual may, after the commencement time, complain to the Commissioner about the act or practice, and the complaint may be dealt with, under the Privacy Act as if those amendments had not been made. (3) Despite the amendments of the Privacy Act made by this Act, the Commissioner may, after the commencement time, investigate the act or practice under subsection 40(2) of the Privacy Act as if those amendments had not been made." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This item applies if:  (a) before the commencement time, an act was done, or a practice was engaged in, by an agency or organisation; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053  Application, transitional and savings provisions  Schedule 6 Provisions relating to other matters  Part 7  Privacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012 Compilation date: 12/3/14 Registered: 6/3/15  (b) the act or practice may be an interference with the privacy of an individual under section 13 or 13A of the Privacy Act (as in force immediately before that time); and  (c) immediately before that time:  (i) the individual has not made a complaint about the act or practice to the Commissioner under section 36 of that Act; and  (ii) the Commissioner has not decided to investigate the act or practice under subsection 40(2) of that Act. (2) Despite the amendments of the Privacy Act made by this Act, the individual may, after the commencement time, complain to the Commissioner about the act or practice, and the complaint may be dealt with, under the Privacy Act as if those amendments had not been made. (3) Despite the amendments of the Privacy Act made by this Act, the Commissioner may, after the commencement time, investigate the act or practice under subsection 40(2) of the Privacy Act as if those amendments had not been made."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "303d7c52620e9eb09d0ec8b6f100b15472f98ce292d0e4b4817c4c4748f2075c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "252"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "An act or practice done before commencement time may be an interference with individual privacy." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.252" ;
    cml:asserts concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-18-2-norm .
